Marloch (Marloch_angry): Something in him finally breaks loose. Of course. Of course, it ends like this. It always does.
Narrator: Catherine's words or choices have undone whatever fragile restraint Marloch had left.
Narrator: He unleashes centuries of fury on Shateroo. Catherine flees, but the town does not survive the night. Homes, streets, the fountain, all of it erased before morning.
